From 2a8f5772272b57d1ed795fa805beab5d087300e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 22:12:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix grid reset bug; add layered payload decoder (base64 +
 zlib + JSON)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Grid reset bug: rowData={[]} in JSX creates a new array literal on every
render, so AgGridReact saw a changed rowData prop and wiped its row model
on every parent re-render — including any click that updated selectedMsg.
Fix: module-level EMPTY_ROWS constant passed as rowData so the reference
never changes after mount; all data management goes through the imperative
API (applyTransaction / setGridOption) exclusively.

Payload decoding (decodePayload.ts):
- For binary payloads (encoding: base64): decode base64 → try gzip/zlib/
  deflate via DecompressionStream (magic-byte priority) → UTF-8 → JSON →
  inner base64 layer (up to depth 4 total).
- For text payloads: fast-path JSON check, then detect base64/base64url and
  run the same pipeline on the decoded bytes.  Only surfaces a result when a
  meaningful transform was achieved (skips showing hex for short strings that
  happen to match the base64 charset).
- Hex dump fallback for payloads that can't be decoded as UTF-8.
DetailPanel shows decode steps as coloured badges (base64 → gzip → json)
with arrows between them. "Copy raw" always copies the original wire value.

